preConditionHook:
// THE NEWEST COMPLETED SWING LEG IS AT LEAST legMultiple TIMES THE MEAN of the
// `numLegs` legs before it on the same side -- an overextension / climax
// warning read with the trend (G03-32, 2 to 3x over five swings) and the
// Anti's change-of-character read against it (G06-34, 1.5x over three). Both
// long sides are "the up-leg exceeds K times the mean of the recent up-legs",
// the same bars, so they are one rule; which context the placement sits in is
// another pane's job. Default 2.0.
//
// LEGS ARE PIVOT TO PIVOT and the ALTERNATION IS GUARDED. On the long side the
// pivots alternate with a swing high NEWEST, so in bars-ago counts (the older
// pivot carries the LARGER count) they descend hiB1 < loB1 < hiB2 < loB2, and
// at numLegs 2 the chain continues < hiB3 < loB3; leg k is
// hiPx(k) - loPx(k). The short side is the same pivots read the other way
// round -- a swing pivot low newest, loB1 < hiB1 < loB2 < hiB2 -- where the
// SAME hiPx(k) - loPx(k) terms are the down-legs. Exactly one ordering can
// hold on any bar, so the two sides never fire together.
//
// THE MEAN IS WRITTEN AS A PRODUCT, division-free:
// legNew * numLegs >= legMultiple * priorSum, with priorSum required POSITIVE
// so the inequality keeps its meaning.
//
// numLegs IS THE NUMBER OF PRIOR LEGS AVERAGED, so numLegs + 1 pivots are
// needed per series and the scan's three-pivot cap (merge decision 14) puts
// numLegs at 1 or 2. A larger value never reaches its pivot count and the rule
// never fires; numLegs below 1 is rejected by the same guard. G03-32's five
// swings and G06-34's three are out of reach and are recorded, not
// approximated.
//
// NOT ShrinkingSwingIncrementsExit, which is the same three-pivot machinery in
// the opposite sense, an EXIT, and a comparison of pivot-to-pivot INCREMENTS
// on ONE series rather than of whole legs across the two. Not
// UpLegsLongerThanDownLegs, which compares with-trend legs against COUNTER
// legs instead of against their own recent mean.
//
// THE PIVOT SCAN IS HAND-ROLLED, not SwingHigh(3, ...): Occurrence 3 and
// beyond is UNMEASURED in the register and numLegs 2 needs a third pivot.
// MEASURED (EL_Swing_Probe.txt / el_swing_output1.txt, @ES 60 min): the pivot
// bar is AT OR BEYOND the `strength` OLDER bars and STRICTLY BEYOND the
// `strength` NEWER bars -- bars-ago indexing makes the SMALLER kk the NEWER
// bar, so the strict half is the kk < jj loop; the confirmation lag is exactly
// `strength` bars, so jj starts there; candidate offsets run 0..Length-1
// inclusive so jj stops at maxBarsBack - 1, while the neighbourhood test
// reaches `strength` bars PAST the window -- deepest bar touched
// maxBarsBack - 1 + strength; scanning newest-first and recording the first
// three hits reproduces Occurrence 1, 2, 3; the comparisons carry the
// 2.22e-12 relational tolerance; the low side's tie sense is the mirror of the
// measured high-side rule. No WFSafe_SwingHigh exists, so plain EL governs.
// Written WITHOUT break, matching the twin statement for statement, and the
// < 3 guards stop a fourth pivot being recorded.
//
// THE SENTINEL IS GUARDED BY THE COUNTS, never by a price test: -1.00 and 0.00
// are legitimate prices in a back-adjusted series. The bar slots carry -1 too,
// and they are bar indices, where -1 is safe.
//
// Every scratch value that must survive the bar is a localVariables entry
// rather than a hook-scope declaration, so the hooks survive a double
// placement; the loop counters and per-candidate flags are block-scoped.
//
// Deepest bar touched: maxBarsBack - 1 + strength.
pivS = (int)strength;
pivW = (int)maxBarsBack;
nHiPiv = 0;
nLoPiv = 0;
hiPx1 = -1.0;
hiPx2 = -1.0;
hiPx3 = -1.0;
loPx1 = -1.0;
loPx2 = -1.0;
loPx3 = -1.0;
hiB1 = -1.0;
hiB2 = -1.0;
hiB3 = -1.0;
loB1 = -1.0;
loB2 = -1.0;
loB3 = -1.0;
for (int jj = pivS; jj <= pivW - 1; ++jj) {
    bool okHi = true;
    bool okLo = true;
    for (int kk = jj - pivS; kk < jj; ++kk) {
        if (!el_gt(high[jj], high[kk])) okHi = false;
        if (!el_lt(low[jj], low[kk])) okLo = false;
    }
    for (int kk = jj + 1; kk <= jj + pivS; ++kk) {
        if (!el_ge(high[jj], high[kk])) okHi = false;
        if (!el_le(low[jj], low[kk])) okLo = false;
    }
    if (okHi && nHiPiv < 3) {
        nHiPiv = nHiPiv + 1;
        if (nHiPiv == 1) { hiPx1 = high[jj]; hiB1 = (double)jj; }
        if (nHiPiv == 2) { hiPx2 = high[jj]; hiB2 = (double)jj; }
        if (nHiPiv == 3) { hiPx3 = high[jj]; hiB3 = (double)jj; }
    }
    if (okLo && nLoPiv < 3) {
        nLoPiv = nLoPiv + 1;
        if (nLoPiv == 1) { loPx1 = low[jj]; loB1 = (double)jj; }
        if (nLoPiv == 2) { loPx2 = low[jj]; loB2 = (double)jj; }
        if (nLoPiv == 3) { loPx3 = low[jj]; loB3 = (double)jj; }
    }
}
legNew = hiPx1 - loPx1;
priorSum = hiPx2 - loPx2;
ordUp = el_lt(hiB1, loB1) && el_lt(loB1, hiB2) && el_lt(hiB2, loB2);
ordDn = el_lt(loB1, hiB1) && el_lt(hiB1, loB2) && el_lt(loB2, hiB2);
if (el_ge(numLegs, 2.0)) {
    priorSum = priorSum + (hiPx3 - loPx3);
    ordUp = ordUp && el_lt(loB2, hiB3) && el_lt(hiB3, loB3);
    ordDn = ordDn && el_lt(hiB2, loB3) && el_lt(loB3, hiB3);
}
haveLegs = el_ge(numLegs, 1.0) && el_ge((double)nHiPiv, numLegs + 1)
    && el_ge((double)nLoPiv, numLegs + 1) && el_gt(priorSum, 0.0);
haveUp = haveLegs && ordUp;
haveDn = haveLegs && ordDn;
